&lt;p&gt;Language quoted from Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS), National Coverage Determinations (NCDs) and coverage provisions in interpretive manuals is italicized throughout the policy. NCDs and coverage provisions in interpretive manuals are not subject to the Local Coverage Determination (LCD) Review Process (42 CFR 405.860[b] and 42 CFR 426 [Subpart D]). In addition, an administrative law judge may not review an NCD. See &amp;sect;1869(f)(1)(A)(i) of the Social Security Act.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Unless otherwise specified, italicized text represents quotation from one or more of the following CMS sources:&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Title XVIII of the Social Security Act (SSA):&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Section 1862(a)(1)(A) excludes expenses incurred for items or services which are not reasonable and necessary for the diagnosis or treatment of illness or injury or to improve the functioning of a malformed body member.&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;Section 1833(e) prohibits Medicare payment for any claim which lacks the necessary information to process the claim. &lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;u&gt;CMS Publications:&lt;&sol;u&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;&lt;br &sol;&gt;CMS Publication 100-04; &lt;em&gt;Medicare Claims Processing Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;, Chapter 13:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;80 Supervision and Interpretation (S &amp;amp; I) Codes and Interventional Radiology&lt;&sol;ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CMS Transmittal No. 423, Publication 100-04, &lt;em&gt;Medicare Claims Processing Manual&lt;&sol;em&gt;, Change Request #3632, January 6, 2005. Update of the Hospital Outpatient Prospective Payment, includes Kyphoplasty.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

indication:
&lt;p dir=&quot;LTR&quot; align=&quot;LEFT&quot;&gt;Provisions in this LCD and related coding article only address Vertebral Augmentation for Osteoporotic Vertebral Compression Fracture (VCF). Coverage will remain available for medically necessary procedures for other conditions not included in this LCD.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p dir=&quot;LTR&quot; align=&quot;LEFT&quot;&gt;PVA (percutaneous vertebroplasty (PVP) or percutaneous kyphoplasty (PKP)) is covered in patients &lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;who qualify based on the following criteria&lt;&sol;span&gt;:&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusion criteria &lt;strong&gt;(ALL are required)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;:
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Acute (&amp;lt; 6 weeks) or subacute (6-12 weeks) osteoporotic VCF (T1 &amp;#8211; L5), based on symptom onset, and documented by advanced imaging (bone marrow edema on MRI or bone-scan&sol;SPECT&sol;CT uptake)&lt;sup&gt;1-3,10,25,27&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Symptomatic (&lt;strong&gt;ONE&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Hospitalized with severe pain (Numeric Rating Scale (NRS) or Visual Analog Scale (VAS) pain score &amp;#8805; 8)&lt;sup&gt;4-7&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Non-hospitalized with moderate to severe pain (NRS or VAS &amp;#8805;5) despite optimal non-surgical management (NSM) (10) (&lt;strong&gt;ONE&lt;&sol;strong&gt;):
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Worsening pain&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Stable to improved pain (but NRS or VAS still &amp;#8805;5) &lt;strong&gt;(with &amp;#8805; 2 of the following):&lt;&sol;strong&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: upper-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Progression of vertebral body height loss&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;gt; 25% vertebral body height reduction&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Kyphotic deformity&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Severe impact of VCF on daily functioning (Roland Morris Disability Questionnaire (RDQ) &amp;gt;17&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Continuum of care&lt;sup&gt;10&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;strong&gt;(Both)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&amp;#160;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;All patients presenting with VCF should be referred for evaluation of BMD and osteoporosis education for subsequent treatment as indicated.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;All patients with VCF should be instructed to take part in an osteoporosis prevention&sol;treatment program.&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exclusion criteria&lt;sup&gt;2,5,8-10:&lt;&sol;sup&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-alpha;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Absolute contraindication:
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current back pain is not primarily due to the identified acute or subacute&amp;#160;VCF(s).&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Osteomyelitis, discitis, active systemic or surgical site infection&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pregnancy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relative contraindication:
&lt;ol style=&quot;list-style-type: lower-roman;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Greater than three vertebral fractures per procedure&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allergy to bone cement or opacification agents&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncorrected coagulopathy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spinal instability&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Myelopathy from the fracture&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Neurologic deficit&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Neural impingement&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fracture retropulsion&sol;canal compromise&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;
